{
  "originalSource": "Kiln log: week A used controller X and recorded 12 cracked tiles in 100. Week B used controller Y and recorded 5 in 100. Clay batches and drying humidity differed between weeks. A same-controller X check also recorded 5 in 100 after a batch change. The team retained Y for a longer trial; it did not conclude that Y caused the reduction. The log contains no long-term durability measurements.",
  "selectedIdea": {
    "title": "Lower cracking merits another trial, not a causal victory",
    "description": "Lower cracking merits another trial, not a causal victory",
    "audience": "Reviewers",
    "rationale": "Preserve observed conclusions and their limits.",
    "evidence": "Y reduced cracks from 12 to 5."
  }
}
